## Tool Routing Hierarchy (STRICT — never skip steps)
1. `anvil_catalog` — check if ANVIL has a component for this task
2. `anvil_dispatch` — route through the hub if a component exists
3. Direct MCP plugin — only if ANVIL has no equivalent
4. Raw API (curl/bash) — only if no MCP exists
5. Browser automation — ABSOLUTE LAST RESORT

Never downgrade silently. Surface errors and fall back only after confirming unreachable.

## Monorepo Structure
```
boz.dev.ANVIL/
  hub/src/index.js          ← hub worker (anvil-hub-mcp)
  components/
    anvil-cloudflare-mcp/   ← CF API, Access, DNS, Gateway (255 tools)
    anvil-clickup-mcp/      ← ClickUp tasks, docs, time
    anvil-github-mcp/       ← GitHub repos, PRs, issues
    anvil-alerts-mcp/       ← ntfy.sh push notifications
    anvil-tessie-mcp/       ← Tesla via Tessie API
    anvil-unifi-mcp/        ← UniFi network
    anvil-ms365-mcp/        ← Microsoft 365
    anvil-gam-mcp/          ← Google Workspace (GAM)
    anvil-elevenlabs-mcp/   ← TTS, voice, transcription
    anvil-legal-scanner/    ← QLD legal sector
    anvil-chrome-devtools-mcp/ ← Browser rendering, Lighthouse
  scripts/
    rotate-hub-api-key.sh
```

